  "label": "Historical Illustration",
  "description": "The image is a 19th-century engraving or lithograph, likely created for publication in a newspaper, magazine, or abolitionist pamphlet. Such illustrations were commonly used to depict the horrors of slavery to sway public opinion and support abolitionist causes. The style and composition are characteristic of moralizing visual propaganda from that era, designed to evoke emotional responses and reinforce narratives of racial injustice.",
